Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: lt9611: preserve the configured I2C address in sleep

The sleep sequence hardcodes the software I2C address to 0x76 (8-bit),
then enables that override. DT510 straps the plain LT9611 to 0x39 (7-bit).
Enabling the override moves it to 0x3b, making subsequent register
accesses at 0x39 fail with -ENXIO until the bridge is reset.

An adapter-scoped trace on build 682 shows the writes to 0x8024 and
0x8023 followed by failed transfers at 0x39 during display-master-only
unbind/rebind. Full bridge reset/reprobe restores video and valid EDID.

Derive the 8-bit software address from the existing I2C client instead
of selecting a different device address. Retain the vendor sleep
sequence and ADDR pin configuration; no startup delay is introduced.
This fixes the address mismatch, not yet the unisolated boot EDID issue.

Selected only for imx8mm-jaguar-dt510 pending broader validation.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Assisted-by: Briar
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/lontium-lt9611.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/lontium-lt9611.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/lontium-lt9611.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/lontium-lt9611.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/lontium-lt9611.c
@@ -468,7 +468,7 @@
 static void lt9611_sleep_setup(struct lt9611 *lt9611)
 {
 	const struct reg_sequence sleep_setup[] = {
-		{ 0x8024, 0x76 },
+		{ 0x8024, lt9611->client->addr << 1 },
 		{ 0x8023, 0x01 },
 		{ 0x8157, 0x03 }, /* set addr pin as output */
 		{ 0x8149, 0x0b },
